{"case_id": "m04", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "qwen__qwen3.6-35b-a3b@low", "model": "qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Whole numbers"], "output": "Average speed = $\\frac{\\text{Total distance}}{\\text{Total time}}$\n\n$= \\frac{240 \\text{ km}}{3 \\text{ h}}$\n\n$= 80 \\text{ km/h}$\n\n**Final answer:** 80 km/h", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 3.763, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 493, "output_tokens": 494, "reasoning_tokens": 428, "cost_usd": 0.000494, "served_models": ["qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b"], "hosts": ["Parasail"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:30:20"}
{"case_id": "m02", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "qwen__qwen3.6-35b-a3b@low", "model": "qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Whole numbers"], "output": "**1. Prime factorisation:**  \n\\(12 = 2^2 \\times 3\\)  \n\\(18 = 2 \\times 3^2\\)  \n\n**2. Apply LCM rule (product of the highest power of each prime factor):**  \n\\(\\text{LCM} = 2^2 \\times 3^2\\)  \n\n**3. Calculate:**  \n\\(\\text{LCM} = 4 \\times 9 = 36\\)  \n\n**Final Answer:** 36", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 10.148, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 407, "output_tokens": 1585, "reasoning_tokens": 1468, "cost_usd": 0.001467, "served_models": ["qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b"], "hosts": ["Parasail"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:30:26"}
{"case_id": "m01", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "qwen__qwen3.6-35b-a3b@low", "model": "qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Whole numbers"], "output": "**Method: Prime Factorisation**\n\n**Step 1: Write each number as a product of prime factors.**\n\n$$84 = 2 \\times 42$$\n$$= 2 \\times 2 \\times 21$$\n$$= 2 \\times 2 \\times 3 \\times 7$$\n$$= 2^2 \\times 3 \\times 7$$\n\n$$126 = 2 \\times 63$$\n$$= 2 \\times 3 \\times 21$$\n$$= 2 \\times 3 \\times 3 \\times 7$$\n$$= 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 7$$\n\n**Step 2: Identify the common prime factors.**\n\n*   Factor 2 appears in both ($2^2$ and $2$). The common factor is **2**.\n*   Factor 3 appears in both ($3$ and $3^2$). The common factor is **3**.\n*   Factor 7 appears in both. The common factor is **7**.\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the HCF.**\n\nMultiply the common prime factors:\n$$HCF = 2 \\times 3 \\times 7$$\n$$HCF = 6 \\times 7$$\n$$HCF = 42$$\n\n**Answer:**\nThe HCF of 84 and 126 is **42**.", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 10.179, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 431, "output_tokens": 1293, "reasoning_tokens": 984, "cost_usd": 0.001207, "served_models": ["qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b"], "hosts": ["Parasail"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:30:26"}
