{"case_id": "m11", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "qwen__qwen3.6-35b-a3b@low", "model": "qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "truncated", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Common Fractions"], "output": "LCM(4, 3) = 12\n\nConvert each fraction to an equivalent fraction with denominator 12:\n\\(\\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{3 \\times 3}{4 \\times 3} = \\frac{9}{12}\\)\n\\(\\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{2 \\times 4}{3 \\times 4} = \\frac{8}{12}\\)\n\nAdd the fractions:\n\\(\\frac{9}{12} + \\frac{8}{12} = \\frac{17}{12}\\)\n\nConvert the improper fraction to a mixed number:\n\\(17 \\div 12 = 1", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 0.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 26.29, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 508, "output_tokens": 2000, "reasoning_tokens": 1843, "cost_usd": 0.001851, "served_models": ["qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b"], "hosts": ["Parasail"], "finish_reasons": ["length"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:07:59"}
{"case_id": "m52", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "qwen__qwen3.6-35b-a3b@low", "model": "qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Functions and inverse functions", "grade12"], "output": "$$f(x) = 3x - 6$$\n\n**Step 1:** Let $y = f(x)$.\n$$y = 3x - 6$$\n\n**Step 2:** Interchange $x$ and $y$.\n$$x = 3y - 6$$\n\n**Step 3:** Make $y$ the subject of the formula.\n$$x + 6 = 3y$$\n$$3y = x + 6$$\n$$y = \\frac{x + 6}{3}$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write in inverse function notation.\n$$\\therefore f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x + 6}{3}$$", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 10.344, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 427, "output_tokens": 1072, "reasoning_tokens": 921, "cost_usd": 0.001007, "served_models": ["qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b"], "hosts": ["AkashML"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:08:03"}
{"case_id": "m46", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "qwen__qwen3.6-35b-a3b@low", "model": "qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Finance, growth and decay", "grade12"], "output": "**Formula:** \\(A = P(1 + i)^n\\)\n\n**Given:**  \n\\(P = 20\\,000\\)  \n\\(r = 9\\% \\text{ p.a.}\\) compounded monthly  \n\\(t = 5 \\text{ years}\\)\n\n**Calculate periodic rate and number of periods:**  \n\\(i = \\dfrac{0.09}{12} = 0.0075\\)  \n\\(n = 5 \\times 12 = 60\\)\n\n**Substitute into formula:**  \n\\(A = 20\\,000(1 + 0.0075)^{60}\\)  \n\\(A = 20\\,000(1.0075)^{60}\\)  \n\\(A = 20\\,000 \\times 1.565681\\ldots\\)  \n\\(A = 31\\,313.62\\)\n\n**Answer:** R31 313.62", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 18.805, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 436, "output_tokens": 1632, "reasoning_tokens": 1387, "cost_usd": 0.001512, "served_models": ["qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b"], "hosts": ["AkashML"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:08:03"}
